## Teardown and verification

| change | restored? |
| --- | --- |
| `no service ssh ip` | yes -- `service ssh ip`, Protocol back to `IPv4,IPv6`, verified on the wire in STEP 6 |
| `no service ssh` | yes -- `service ssh`, Enabled, verified on the wire by the probe and by the final running-config |
| `port1.0.2` trunk/vlan 60 (collateral of the refused batch) | yes -- rebuilt and verified with a 3/3 ping to swi_b |
| startup-config | **never written in this case** |

**The DUT's running-config is byte-identical before and after the case.** `python3
tools/rcdiff.py <pre-step show running-config> <post-step show running-config>`: **no output,
exit 0**.

While checking that, one false alarm is worth recording so the next tester does not chase it:
`show running-config | include service ssh|allow-users` appeared to be missing the `service ssh`
line after the off/on cycle. It was not -- the running-config prints
`ssh server allow-users manager` **before** `service ssh`, and a local `head -8` had cut the
second line off. Re-read deliberately:
```
awplus# show running-config | include service ssh
service ssh
awplus# show running-config | include service ssh|allow-users
ssh server allow-users manager
service ssh
```
**The AW+ alternation filter behaved correctly here.** This is not another instance of the
section 7G defect; that one is specifically a chained `| exclude` after `| include`.

